deployments/
# ...but `deployments/` is unanchored, so it also swallows any directory of
# that name anywhere in the tree. experiments/021-state-machines/deployments/
# is the deployment-lifecycle state model, not a deployment worktree.
!experiments/021-state-machines/deployments/

# Runtime state, tracked by mistake. Same defect class as ports.tsv: a file that
# a running process writes has no business in git -- it is stale the moment it
# is committed, and it makes every checkout disagree with every host.
targets/bastille/front/tmp/*.pid
targets/node/.*.log
targets/node/live

# The port registry is per-HOST runtime state, not repo content. Every host has
# different allocations, and targets/node/deploy.sh writes a row on every deploy,
# so a tracked copy is stale the moment it is committed and blocks a rebase every
# time anything deploys. Fourth instance of this defect today after front.pid,
# targets/node/live and this file earlier. A CMDB does not live in the app repo.
ports.tsv

# The local IDP calendar: per-host state, which slots THIS machine granted and
# which checks it saw clear. Fifth instance of the rule -- a CMDB does not live
# in the app repo (ports.tsv, front.pid, targets/node/live).
.idp/
research/build/
.DS_Store
research/appendix/
